{
  "case_id": "2018-18-481",
  "document_hash": "83a93e514b16a4d4fa1190e1002a4035f0b1450385a09e79c19c5b8dc8611717",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-18-481",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "83a93e514b16a4d4fa1190e1002a4035f0b1450385a09e79c19c5b8dc8611717",
      "evidence_id": "ev-83a93e514b16-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:05 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Food Marketing Institute",
      "case_id": "2018-18-481",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "83a93e514b16a4d4fa1190e1002a4035f0b1450385a09e79c19c5b8dc8611717",
      "evidence_id": "ev-83a93e514b16-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, our injury in fact is the disclosure of our members' store-level sales information that they keep secret."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-18-481",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "83a93e514b16a4d4fa1190e1002a4035f0b1450385a09e79c19c5b8dc8611717",
      "evidence_id": "ev-83a93e514b16-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Not if the government decides that it doesn't want to give"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Food Marketing Institute",
      "case_id": "2018-18-481",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "83a93e514b16a4d4fa1190e1002a4035f0b1450385a09e79c19c5b8dc8611717",
      "evidence_id": "ev-83a93e514b16-0000-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If this Court reverses, the only thing that will lead to our information certainly being made public will be destroyed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2018-18-481",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "83a93e514b16a4d4fa1190e1002a4035f0b1450385a09e79c19c5b8dc8611717",
      "evidence_id": "ev-83a93e514b16-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So, as I understood your brief, and tell me if I've gotten this wrong, you're basically saying that the first way of showing confidentiality, the non-assurances way --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Robert M. Loeb",
      "case_id": "2018-18-481",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "83a93e514b16a4d4fa1190e1002a4035f0b1450385a09e79c19c5b8dc8611717",
      "evidence_id": "ev-83a93e514b16-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If the Court reaches the merits here, it should affirm the judgment of the Eighth Circuit. For 45 years, the language of Exemption 4 has been properly construed to require a showing of likely competitive harm. Not only is that competitive harm standard fully supported by the common law that prevailed in 1966 when Exemption 4 was enacted, the standard has also been ratified by Congress for reasons that I'll explain."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-18-481",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "83a93e514b16a4d4fa1190e1002a4035f0b1450385a09e79c19c5b8dc8611717",
      "evidence_id": "ev-83a93e514b16-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'm sorry, do you accept the reasonable possibility of harm test?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-18-481",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "83a93e514b16a4d4fa1190e1002a4035f0b1450385a09e79c19c5b8dc8611717",
      "evidence_id": "ev-83a93e514b16-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Is it them or other courts?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2018-18-481",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "83a93e514b16a4d4fa1190e1002a4035f0b1450385a09e79c19c5b8dc8611717",
      "evidence_id": "ev-83a93e514b16-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: What if the standard were that the -- the agency must"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-18-481",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "83a93e514b16a4d4fa1190e1002a4035f0b1450385a09e79c19c5b8dc8611717",
      "evidence_id": "ev-83a93e514b16-0002-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the district court found that the evidence presented by the government and by FMI to show harm was -- was speculative at best and marginal at best."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2018-18-481",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "83a93e514b16a4d4fa1190e1002a4035f0b1450385a09e79c19c5b8dc8611717",
      "evidence_id": "ev-83a93e514b16-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: May -- may I ask, Mr. Loeb, if -- if I were to say to you give me your best shot on a textual argument for your position, so putting aside subsequent congressional inaction, putting aside how many courts have adopted this test, just sort of give me your best shot for why this is the right way to read the text, what would you say?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2018-18-481",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "83a93e514b16a4d4fa1190e1002a4035f0b1450385a09e79c19c5b8dc8611717",
      "evidence_id": "ev-83a93e514b16-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: So how many -- how many courts of appeals do you have to take -- I assume uniform isn't enough -- if there are just two, that's uniform, but you have -- I understand you -- you think you have eight, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-18-481",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "83a93e514b16a4d4fa1190e1002a4035f0b1450385a09e79c19c5b8dc8611717",
      "evidence_id": "ev-83a93e514b16-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Counsel, that -- that begs a question, which is we sort of"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Evan A. Young (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2018-18-481",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "83a93e514b16a4d4fa1190e1002a4035f0b1450385a09e79c19c5b8dc8611717",
      "evidence_id": "ev-83a93e514b16-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Of course, our clients aren't paying for us to pursue this to this level because they just feel like it. Of course, we think there's substantial competitive harm."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Evan A. Young (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2018-18-481",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "83a93e514b16a4d4fa1190e1002a4035f0b1450385a09e79c19c5b8dc8611717",
      "evidence_id": "ev-83a93e514b16-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And then, lastly, it has to be confidential or privileged. And all that Congress asked the courts to do is answer the objective question: Does the person whose information the government now has, does that person keep this secret and not publicly disclose it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2018-18-481",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "83a93e514b16a4d4fa1190e1002a4035f0b1450385a09e79c19c5b8dc8611717",
      "evidence_id": "ev-83a93e514b16-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: But why not call it harm, some harm, I mean, some harm, because Congress doesn't go around protecting people from X where X doesn't cause any harm."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-18-481",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "83a93e514b16a4d4fa1190e1002a4035f0b1450385a09e79c19c5b8dc8611717",
      "evidence_id": "ev-83a93e514b16-0003-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
